<section class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-tp-green-light">
  <div class="max-w-site mx-auto px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-tp-text text-center mb-10">
        Built by someone who gets it
      </h2>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-tp-lg border border-tp-border/50 shadow-tp p-8 md:p-10">
        <blockquote class="text-tp-muted leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            Hi, I'm Emma. My partner Patrick recently had a liver transplant, and I saw first-hand how much there was to keep track of in those early days — medications, vitals, symptoms, clinic questions — all while dealing with sleep deprivation, fatigue, and brain fog.
          </p>
          <p>
            I wanted to lighten the load and help him focus on what really mattered: getting better.
          </p>
          <p>
            I built Transplant Log after seeing his day-to-day needs and hearing what his clinicians wanted to know from him at each appointment. It started as something just for us, but I'm sharing it because I hope it can help other families going through the same thing.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-tp-border">
          <p class="font-semibold text-tp-text">Emma</p>
          <p class="text-tp-muted text-sm">Creator of Transplant Log</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
